# A wrong move the record answers: the refutation is played.
#
# Collections mark a move BM and record how it is punished. That answer was left
# lying in the file — the solver was told "Wrong" and never shown why, which is
# the whole of what a wrong move has to teach. The correct path already played
# the recorded reply; this branch simply never called the same navigateForward().
#
# No engine is involved. What to do when the record has *no* refutation is a
# separate question and stays on request (Space).
#
#   ./tests/run_scenarios.sh tests/scenarios/tsumego_refutation.scn

new_game 9
wait_idle
load_tsumego tests/data/tsumego_refuted.sgf
wait_idle
expect mode tsumego
expect tsumego true
expect move_count 0
expect white_stones 5

# a8 is the wrong move, recorded as BM with White's answer after it.
click 0 1
click 0 1
wait_until msg tsumego_wrong

# Two moves, not one: the mistake and its punishment. The white stone is the
# refutation actually played onto the board.
expect move_count 2
expect white_stones 6

# And the verdict survives the navigation that played it — setting it before
# navigateForward() lost it, leaving the punishment with nothing to explain it.
expect msg tsumego_wrong

# The refutation's own comment is what says why, so it must be on screen.
expect comment and this is how it is punished
